# snip-it's SIX REAL e2e tests, re-expressed as behaviour trees.
#
# Not invented. Every step below corresponds to a line that exists today in
# snip-it frontend/e2e/editor.spec.ts on origin/dev. The point of encoding the
# real suite rather than a toy is that the generated output can be compared
# against hand-written code that a person actually wrote and CI actually runs.
#
# `contract` steps are the honest part: they are assertions the tree CANNOT
# express, kept in so the coverage number is not flattered by omitting them.

# ── features (snip-it.notes.md 2026-10-20 22:42Z: "snip it needs feature organisation") ──
# The grouping is the agent's reading of that note: deny it if it is the wrong cut.
feature FEAT-EDITOR "The web editor: upload a take, transcribe it, cut words and pauses, export"
feature FEAT-TELEPROMPTER "The iPhone teleprompter app: read the script, record the take, send it to snip-it"

behaviour BEH-HOME-1 "The landing page renders"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Home
  then sees region:Main

behaviour BEH-EDIT-1 "The editor loads a transcript and offers its toolbar"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  given transcription:Completed
  when opens page:TranscriptEditor
  then sees button:SelectAll
  then sees button:RemoveFillerWords
  then sees button:SendForExport
  then shows region:WordTrack "transcribe"

behaviour BEH-EDIT-2 "The editor can be switched to dark mode"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  given transcription:Completed
  when opens page:TranscriptEditor
  then sees button:SelectAll
  when activates button:ToggleTheme

behaviour BEH-CUT-1 "Sending for export submits a cut and surfaces the finished job"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  given transcription:Completed
  when opens page:TranscriptEditor
  when activates button:RemoveFillerWords
  when activates button:SendForExport
  then shows region:CutStatus "is complete"
  then sees link:Download
  contract POST /api/cuts is sent exactly once
  contract the body carries transcriptionJobId
  contract the body carries every word
  contract at least one word is marked not kept

behaviour BEH-UP-1 "Uploading a file transcribes it and opens the editor"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Upload
  then sees heading:TranscribeAVideo
  when fills form:Upload with ?fields
  when activates button:Transcribe
  then sees button:SelectAll
  then lands on page:TranscriptEditor
  contract the upload is multipart/form-data
  contract the request path is /snipit/api/transcriptions

behaviour BEH-FILL-1 "Removing filler words leaves the editor interactive"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  given transcription:Completed
  when opens page:TranscriptEditor
  when activates button:RemoveFillerWords
  then sees button:SendForExport

# ── the unknowns mechanism, on real material ──
# BEH-UP-1 above says "fills the upload form" and glosses over WHICH fields —
# exactly James's "user fills out x form. This is ok but this creates unknowns."
# It is answered not by asking the author, but by a DIFFERENT behaviour that
# happens to name the field. That is the whole cross-resolution idea, and the
# field name below is the real one from editor.spec.ts (`getByLabel(...)`).

behaviour BEH-UP-2 "The upload form takes a single video or audio file"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  when opens page:Upload
  when attaches file:talk_mp4 to field:VideoOrAudioFile
  provides form:Upload.fields = VideoOrAudioFile

# The editor's route carries an id. That is a hole too, and the generator refuses
# to emit `./editor/` rather than quietly produce a test that navigates nowhere.
# Supplying it is the same mechanism as any other unknown — one symbol table.
behaviour BEH-EDIT-0 "The editor addresses one transcription by id"
  in FEAT-EDITOR
  actor visitor
  provides page:TranscriptEditor.transcriptionId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

# ── the video pipeline (claude-code-bot#114, 2026-10-18) ──
# James: "i want that video pipeline software that we envisioned… even if it is just
# beginning to plan videos and scripts there or reviewing what the pipeline / boards
# look like". Nothing had been specced for it, so everything below is INFERRED and
# unreviewed: a proposal for him to approve or deny in Kit, not a decision.

feature FEAT-PIPELINE "The video pipeline: every video from idea to published, on one board"

behaviour BEH-PIPE-1 "A board shows every video as a card in one of five stages: Idea, Scripted, Recorded, Cut, Published"
  in FEAT-PIPELINE
  layer ux
  source inferred claude-code-bot#114
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor creator
  contract "reviewing what the pipeline / boards look like": the board is the first screen, so the pipeline is visible before any content exists
  contract the five stages are a guess at his flow, from note to upload; he can rename, add or drop a stage
  contract the board is saved in the creator's browser, like the footage (snip-it#22): snip-it has no sign-in, so a server-side board would be readable by anyone with the link

behaviour BEH-PIPE-2 "A creator adds a video idea as a card with a working title and a few lines of notes"
  in FEAT-PIPELINE
  layer ux
  source inferred claude-code-bot#114
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor creator
  contract "beginning to plan videos": an idea needs only a title, so capturing one takes seconds
  contract a new card lands in Idea

behaviour BEH-PIPE-3 "A creator writes a video's script on its card, and the card moves to Scripted"
  in FEAT-PIPELINE
  layer ux
  source inferred claude-code-bot#114
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor creator
  contract "plan videos and scripts there": the script is plain text, edited in the browser and saved with the card
  contract a card moves stage by the creator's choice; nothing moves it behind his back

behaviour BEH-PIPE-4 "The teleprompter app opens a card's script, so the words are written once"
  in FEAT-PIPELINE
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer technical
  source inferred claude-code-bot#114
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  pending
  actor creator
  contract the iPhone teleprompter (claude-code-bot#105) reads the script from the card instead of a pasted copy
  contract a take recorded against a card moves it to Recorded

behaviour BEH-PIPE-5 "A recorded take is cut in the editor from its card, and the card moves to Cut"
  in FEAT-PIPELINE
  layer ux
  source inferred claude-code-bot#114
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor creator
  contract the card links to the existing upload, transcribe and cut flow (BEH-UP-1, BEH-CUT-1) rather than rebuilding it
  contract the browser holds the video (snip-it#22), so the card keeps only the take's transcript id: never the footage, nor the export link (single-use, deleted as it streams), nor the edits (the editor reloads every word kept)
  contract a transcribed take moves the card to Recorded and a finished export moves it to Cut; neither ever moves a card backwards

behaviour BEH-PIPE-6 "A creator marks a video Published with its link, so the board records what shipped"
  in FEAT-PIPELINE
  layer ux
  source inferred claude-code-bot#114
  review unreviewed
  priority 3
  actor creator
  contract publishing stays manual (a pasted YouTube link); posting to YouTube for him is out of scope

# ── the teleprompter app (snip-it.notes.md, 2026-10-20 22:43–22:45Z) ──
# James, on the first TestFlight build: "it looks incredible as a tele prompter but
# currently the speach models arent loading". Every behaviour below is from those
# notes; the contracts are the agent's reading of them, unreviewed.

behaviour BEH-TELE-1 "Speech models are managed in Settings: listed, downloaded with progress, and deleted"
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer ux
  source defined snip-it.notes.md#2026-10-20-2243
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor creator
  contract "model management in settings rather than it just trying to download when you hit prompt": the prompter never starts a download
  contract each model shows its state: not downloaded, downloading with a percentage, preparing, ready, or failed with the reason
  contract the list is the English models (tiny, base, small) that WhisperKit says this iPhone can run
  contract a ready model can be deleted to free space, and the chosen model is the one the prompter uses

behaviour BEH-TELE-2 "When the speech model cannot load, the prompter says why and still works by hand"
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer ux
  source defined snip-it.notes.md#2026-10-20-2243
  review unreviewed
  priority 1
  actor creator
  contract "some errors messages when this happens": the message names the step that failed (download, preparing, listening) and carries the engine's own reason
  contract with no model downloaded, the prompter points to Settings instead of downloading
  contract recording and tapping a line to move on keep working without speech

behaviour BEH-TELE-3 "A take can be watched in the app"
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer ux
  source defined snip-it.notes.md#2026-10-20-2245
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  actor creator
  contract "in app video viewing": tapping a take plays it full screen with the system player, original or cut

behaviour BEH-TELE-4 "The prompter has camera controls: zoom, tap to focus and expose, front or back camera"
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer ux
  source defined snip-it.notes.md#2026-10-20-2244
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  pending
  actor creator
  contract "I would like some camera controls": which controls is the agent's guess; he can add or drop any

behaviour BEH-TELE-5 "On an iPhone 17, the front camera records a landscape take while the phone is held upright"
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer ux
  source defined snip-it.notes.md#2026-10-20-2244
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  pending
  actor creator
  contract "use the iphone 17s landscape selfie video recording": the square Center Stage sensor is cropped to 16:9 through AVFoundation's dynamic aspect ratio (iOS 26)
  contract on a phone without that camera the choice is hidden, not shown disabled
  contract the script stays at the top of the upright screen, nearest the lens, in both shapes

behaviour BEH-TELE-6 "TestFlight builds come from a release branch, not from every push to dev"
  in FEAT-TELEPROMPTER
  layer technical
  source defined snip-it.notes.md#2026-10-20-2243
  review unreviewed
  priority 2
  pending
  actor creator
  contract "maybe we need a ios release branch": Codemagic builds pushes to ios-release that change ios/; dev keeps the unsigned compile check only
  contract a Codemagic change is a platform change (claude-code-bot#83), so it goes up as its own pull request for James to merge
